"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KQSRWYTB1S0R69E\",\"title\":\"Murudagiri Biochar Project — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Murudagiri Biochar Project\",\"Equilibrium\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"2W49\",\"Crediting period\",\"20 May 2026 to 20 May 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"2W49\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"25 Jun 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"12 Jun 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://equilibriumearth.com\",\"t\":\"Equilibrium\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1KQSRWYTB1S0R69E/pjd_1KVZTQHFP1S0MJJC/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K3PCHYCA1S0VE66/prj_1KQSRWYTB1S0R69E/pjd_1KTY70DXW1S02MWH/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nMurudagiri Biochar Project\\nEquilibrium\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n2W49\\nCrediting period\\n20 May 2026 to 20 May 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nThe Murudagiri Biochar Project converts regionally abundant and underutilized biomass, including corn cob residues and invasive species such as Prosopis Juliflora into durable biochar. By diverting biomass from unmanaged decay pathways, the facility stabilizes biogenic carbon into long-lived soil carbon pools that reduces particulate pollution and supports ecosystem restoration.\\n\\nGadag, Karnataka\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 21 Jun 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2026\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n25 Jun 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n12 Jun 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"